{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe journey from Brussels to Bruges was a study in contrasts. I left Cousin in Brussels on Friday, viewing the Ghent Altarpiece fragments before boarding a canal barge. It was a strange vessel: while the water lapped against the hull, the cabin filled with the sharp clatter of whist and the rustle of newspapers. I found myself observing how men seek distraction in the small, even as the river carries them toward the great.\n\nWe arrived in Bruges at eight, the evening air cool and damp. I am resting now, tired but content. The landscape here is flat, yet the history feels heavy, almost suffocating in its density. I think of our home, of the quiet order we have built, and how different it is from this transient, noisy passage. I hope you and the boys are well. I miss your company and the silence of our study.\n\nYours ever,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080627,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":200,"prompt_tokens":937,"total_tokens":1137,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-F6b3yqHiwO5x4vvy7SMkR3bmWgnRCty8","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":937,"prompt_ms":994.9,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0617929562433297,"prompt_per_second":941.8031963011359,"predicted_n":200,"predicted_ms":4821.703,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.22966331658292,"predicted_per_second":41.27172494863329}}